@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "provisioning.user.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Provisioning Worker Integration
	Testing to assure that koroneiki account worker information transfers properly to the account index.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | usr.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | USR                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | usr.koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | usr.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | USR                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | usr.koroneiki3                       |
	| Email Address | usr.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | USR                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki3                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | usr.koroneiki4                       |
	| Email Address | usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | USR                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki4                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | usr.koroneiki5                       |
	| Email Address | usr.koroneiki5@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | USR                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki5                           |
	| Email Status  | UNVERIFIED                           |

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Korusr - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Oneusr - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Usrkor - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the third default user ID variable
	* I tear down the teams on koroneiki with the following names
	| User Site Partner |
	| Changed Partner   |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korusr - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Oneusr - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Usrkor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| USRKORKORUSR |
	| ONEUSRONEUSR |
	| USRKOR       |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| USRKORKORUSR |
	| ONEUSRONEUSR |
	| USRKOR       |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki5@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki5@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki5@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki5@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contact roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Liferay User Worker Role |
	| Second User Worker Role  |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Korusr - ${staticProjectName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Usrkor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki3@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| usr.koroneiki5@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Korusr - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Oneusr - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Usrkor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId3}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View worker
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Testing the ability to create a worker in koroneiki and viewing the respective worker in the provisioning account details page

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Usrkor - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | USR                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | USR                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki4                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Korusr - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I create a team with the name "User Site Partner" for the account "Korusr - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I assign the team with the name "User Site Partner" on the account "Korusr - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner            |
	| First Line Support |
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the team "User Site Partner"
	| usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the Liferay worker role for accounts |
	| Name        | Liferay User Worker Role                     |
	| Type        | Account Worker                               |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "usr.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Korusr - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Liferay User Worker Role |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticKoroneikiAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticKoroneikiAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korusr"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korusr - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Contacts" tab
	Then I should be able to view the contact with the email address "usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Name          | USR Koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Role          | Support Watcher                      |
	| User Status   | VERIFIED                             |
	And I should not be able to view the contact with the email address "usr.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	When I click on the "Liferay Workers" tab
	Then I should be able to view the worker with the email address "usr.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Name          | USR Koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | usr.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Role          | Liferay User Worker Role             |
	| User Status   | VERIFIED                             |
	And I should not be able to view the worker with the email address "usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	When I click on the "History" tab
	Then the history entry with the keywords "Auto > Assigned Contact" and "USR Koroneiki1" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Assigned Contact > USR Koroneiki1 |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                             |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                      |
	| Update Field New Value      | Support Watcher                          |
	And the history entry with the keywords "Koroneiki QA Service Producer > Assigned Contact" and "USR Koroneiki2" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Koroneiki QA Service Producer > Assigned Contact > USR Koroneiki2 |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                                                      |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                               |
	| Update Field New Value      | Liferay User Worker Role                                          |

Scenario: View owner worker
	Testing the ability to create an owner worker via Dossiera and viewing the respective worker in the provisioning account details page

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Usrkor - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | USR                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | USR                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki4                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Korusr - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I create a team with the name "User Site Partner" for the account "Korusr - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I assign the team with the name "User Site Partner" on the account "Korusr - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner            |
	| First Line Support |
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the team "User Site Partner"
	| usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticKoroneikiAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticKoroneikiAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korusr"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korusr - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Contacts" tab
	Then I should be able to view the contact with the email address "usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Name          | USR Koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Role          | Support Watcher                      |
	| User Status   | VERIFIED                             |
	And I should not be able to view the contact with the email address "usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	When I click on the "Liferay Workers" tab
	Then I should be able to view the worker with the email address "usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Name          | USR Koroneiki4                       |
	| Email Address | usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Role          | Liferay Sales                        |
	| Role          | Secondary Contact                    |
	| User Status   | VERIFIED                             |
	And I should not be able to view the worker with the email address "usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	When I click on the "History" tab
	Then the history entry number "1" with the keyword "Auto > Assigned Contact" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Assigned Contact > USR Koroneiki4 |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                             |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                      |
	| Update Field New Value      | Liferay Sales                            |
	And the history entry number "2" with the keyword "Auto > Assigned Contact" with the field value "Contact Role" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Assigned Contact > USR Koroneiki4 |
	| Update Field Name           | Contact Role                             |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                      |
	| Update Field New Value      | Secondary Contact                        |

Scenario: View owner worker as primary contact
	Testing the ability to create an owner worker via Dossiera and adding the primary contact role and viewing the respective worker in the provisioning account details page

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Usrkor - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | USR                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | USR                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki4                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Korusr - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I create a team with the name "User Site Partner" for the account "Korusr - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I assign the team with the name "User Site Partner" on the account "Korusr - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner            |
	| First Line Support |
	And I assign contacts with the following email addresses to the team "User Site Partner"
	| usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Korusr - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Primary Contact |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticKoroneikiAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticKoroneikiAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korusr"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korusr - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	Then I should be able to view the following account values in the account details page
	| Name            | Korusr - ${staticProjectName}        |
	| Code            | USRKORKORUSR                         |
	| State           | ACTIVE                               |
	| Support Region  | United States                        |
	| SLA             | Platinum                             |
	| FLS Partner     | User Site Partner                    |
	| Primary Contact | usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	When I click on the "Contacts" tab
	Then I should be able to view the contact with the email address "usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Name          | USR Koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Role          | Support Watcher                      |
	| User Status   | VERIFIED                             |
	And I should not be able to view the contact with the email address "usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	When I click on the "Liferay Workers" tab
	Then I should be able to view the worker with the email address "usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Name          | USR Koroneiki4                       |
	| Email Address | usr.koroneiki4@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Role          | Liferay Sales                        |
	| Role          | Primary Contact                      |
	| Role          | Secondary Contact                    |
	| User Status   | VERIFIED                             |
	And I should not be able to view the worker with the email address "usr.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken"

